    {
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "P8E80F9AEF21F6940" },
      "description": "Chronological, one row per step, prefixed with chat + a short id (first 8 chars of the trigger-scoped part of `turn`) so same-turn rows stay identifiable even when other chats' turns interleave — or use the $Chat filter above to isolate one chat entirely. A reserved 2-character direction column on every row keeps the ┌ │ └ tree frame aligned: » marks the incoming request, « marks the row pan-agent actually sent to Telegram (evt=\"reply_sent\"). `note` rows are mid-turn assistant commentary (evt=\"assistant\") — genuinely distinct from `reply`, which comes from the real delivery decision the runner logs at send time, not guessed from assistant text. `mute` rows (evt=\"reply_muted\") show why a turn stayed silent (task_no_update / empty) plus whatever reasoning the model wrote before going quiet — `note` and `mute` never get «, nothing was sent for those. Turns logged before this row format shipped (2026-08-24) have no reply_sent/reply_muted events and render with no reply/mute row and no «.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 35, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "id": 11,
      "options": {
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "enableInfiniteScrolling": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "showControls": false,
        "showTime": true,
        "sortOrder": "Ascending",
        "unwrappedColumns": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.2",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "P8E80F9AEF21F6940" },
          "direction": "backward",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{namespace=\"pan-agent\", pod=~\"$Chat\"} | json | evt=~\"user|tool_use|assistant|reply_sent|reply_muted|turn_end\" | line_format `{{ $rid := regexReplaceAll \"^[a-z]+:([^:-]+).*\" .turn \"${1}\" | trunc 8 }}{{ $pfx := printf \"%-17s%-9s\" .person $rid }}{{ if eq .evt \"user\" }}{{ $t := regexReplaceAll \"^@\\\\S+:\\\\s*\" .text \"\" }}{{ $t = regexReplaceAll \"^\\\\[Scheduled task [^\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\" $t \"\" }}{{ $t = regexReplaceAll \"\\\\s+\" $t \" \" }}{{ $pfx }}» ┌ message {{ $t | trunc 160 }}{{ else if eq .evt \"tool_use\" }}{{ $in := .input }}{{ if hasPrefix \"{\\\"command\\\"\" $in }}{{ $in = (fromJson $in).command }}{{ else if hasPrefix \"{\\\"skill\\\"\" $in }}{{ $in = (fromJson $in).skill }}{{ end }}{{ $pfx }}  │ {{ printf \"%-7s\" (.tool | lower) }} {{ regexReplaceAll \"\\\\s+\" $in \" \" | trunc 100 }}{{ else if eq .evt \"assistant\" }}{{ $pfx }}  │ {{ printf \"%-7s\" \"note\" }} {{ regexReplaceAll \"\\\\s+\" .text \" \" | trunc 120 }}{{ else if eq .evt \"reply_sent\" }}{{ $pfx }}« │ {{ printf \"%-7s\" \"reply\" }} {{ regexReplaceAll \"\\\\s+\" .text \" \" | trunc 120 }}{{ else if eq .evt \"reply_muted\" }}{{ $pfx }}  │ {{ printf \"%-7s\" \"mute\" }} ({{ .reason }}) {{ regexReplaceAll \"\\\\s+\" .text \" \" | trunc 120 }}{{ else if eq .evt \"turn_end\" }}{{ $pfx }}  └ {{ if eq .ok \"true\" }}✓ ok{{ else }}✗ fail{{ end }} · {{ .turns }} steps · ${{ .cost_usd }} · {{ add (int .inputTokens) (int .outputTokens) }} tok · {{ printf \"%.1fs\" (divf (float64 .dur_ms) 1000) }}{{ if and (eq .ok \"false\") .error }} · {{ .error | trunc 80 }}{{ end }}{{ else }}{{ $pfx }}  │ {{ .evt }}  {{ .text }}{{ end }}`",
          "queryType": "range",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Logs",
